-- Migration 23: annotation tags — freeform grouping tags on source_annotation.
--
-- source_annotation is SCHEMAFULL, so a new field must be DEFINEd here (a
-- Pydantic-only field would be dropped on save). Mirrors migration 17's
-- pattern for adding a collection field to a SCHEMAFULL table
-- (chat_tag_colors ON notebook).
--
-- CORRECTION (live-verified): a DEFINE FIELD with DEFAULT does NOT backfill
-- existing rows. Rows created before this migration keep `tags` as NONE (not
-- []), which then breaks any UPDATE of that row (the SCHEMAFULL field has no
-- value to satisfy). Migration 24 fixes this with an explicit backfill
-- (`UPDATE source_annotation SET tags = [] WHERE tags IS NONE`).
--
-- tags: a plain array of strings the user attaches to a highlight (e.g.
-- "Important", "Question", chapter names). Auto-colored on the frontend from
-- the tag text; no per-tag color state is stored server-side.
--
-- NOTE: the element type `array<string>` is REQUIRED. An untyped `TYPE array`
-- silently drops the array's contents on write in this SurrealDB build (stores
-- []); only a typed array (or FLEXIBLE, as `rect` uses for opaque dicts)
-- preserves the elements.

DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS tags ON TABLE source_annotation TYPE array<string> DEFAULT [];
